{{!
    @template local_oksigeniamarandu/telegram_sketch

    A sketch of the talk with @BotFather, which answers in English: the name, the username and the token, pointed out.
    Not a screenshot, so that it does not age.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * sketch - name, user and token, of example.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "sketch": {"name": "Example School", "user": "example_bot", "token": "123:ABC"}
    }
}}
{{#sketch}}
<ol class="mrd-bf">
    <li class="me"><span class="b">/newbot</span></li>
    <li lang="en"><span class="b">Alright, a new bot. … Please choose a name for your bot.</span></li>
    <li class="me"><span class="b">{{name}}</span><span class="ann">{{#str}} telegram:sketch:name, local_oksigeniamarandu {{/str}}</span></li>
    <li lang="en"><span class="b">Good. Now let's choose a username for your bot. It must end in `bot`…</span></li>
    <li class="me"><span class="b">{{user}}</span><span class="ann">{{#str}} telegram:sketch:user, local_oksigeniamarandu {{/str}}</span></li>
    <li><span class="b" lang="en">Done! Congratulations on your new bot. … Use this token to access the HTTP API:<mark>{{token}}</mark>Keep your token secure…</span><span class="ann">{{#str}} telegram:sketch:token, local_oksigeniamarandu {{/str}}</span></li>
</ol>
{{/sketch}}
